===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*terh₂-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|entren}}, from {{der|en|fro|entrer}}, from {{der|en|la|intrō|t=enter|pos=verb}}, from {{m|la|intrā||inside}}. Has been spelled as "enter" for several centuries even in the United Kingdom, although British English and the English of many Commonwealth Countries (e.g. Australia, Canada) retain the "re" ending for many words such as [[centre]], [[fibre]], [[spectre]], [[theatre]], [[calibre]], [[sombre]], [[lustre]], and [[litre]].

