===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[go]] or [[come]] into an enclosed or partially enclosed space.
#: {{ux|en|You should knock before you '''enter''', unless you want to see me naked.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1555|author=John Proctor|page=86
|title=The historie of Wyates rebellion, with the order and maner of resisting the same,&nbsp;&hellip;
|url=http://books.google.com/books?id=YQ2gAAAAMAAJ&pg=PT186&dq=%22to+enter%22&lr=lang_en&as_drrb_is=b&as_minm_is=0&as_miny_is=1550&as_maxm_is=0&as_maxy_is=1560&as_brr=1&cd=1#v=onepage&q=%22to%20enter%22&f=false
|passage={{...}}you can fynde in youre heartes to assaulte her with rebellion, or in any wise [ways] suffer any one eyvil motion '''to enter''' into your thoughtes against her?}}
#* {{RQ:King James Version|John|3|5|passage=Except a man be born of water and of the Spirit, he cannot '''enter''' into the kingdom of God.}}
#* {{RQ:Besant Ivory Gate|III
|passage=In former days every tavern of repute kept such a room for its own select circle, a club, or society, of habitués, who met every evening, for a pipe and a cheerful glass.{{...}}Strangers might '''enter''' the room, but they were made to feel that they were there on sufferance: they were received with distance and suspicion.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2024|author=NTSB| title=Intersection Crash Between Passenger Car and Combination Vehicle, Tishomingo, Oklahoma, March 22, 2022
| passage= We determined that the car driver’s transportation of multiple teen passengers, limited driving experience, and likely impairment from effects of cannabis at the time of the crash adversely affected her judgment of the danger of '''entering''' the intersection in front of the approaching combination vehicle.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To cause to go (into), or to be received (into); to put in; to insert; to cause to be admitted.
#: {{ux|en|to '''enter''' a knife into a piece of wood}}
#: {{ux|en|to '''enter''' a boy at college, a horse for a race, etc.}}
# {{lb|en|figuratively}} To [[go]] or [[come]] into (a state or profession).
#: {{ux|en|My twelve-year-old son will be '''entering''' his teens next year.}}
#: {{ux|en|She had planned to '''enter''' the legal profession.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2013-06-28|author=w:Joris Luyendijk
|volume=189|issue=3|page=21|magazine=w:The Guardian Weekly
|title=Our banks are out of control
|url=http://www.guardian.co.uk/commentisfree/joris-luyendijk-banking-blog/2013/jun/19/banking-britain-beyond-control
|passage=Until 2008 there was denial over what finance had become.&nbsp;&hellip;&nbsp; But the scandals kept coming, and so we '''entered''' stage three – what therapists call "bargaining".}}
# {{senseid|en|type into a computer}} {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[type]] (something) into a [[computer]]; to [[input#Verb|input]].
#: {{ux|en|'''Enter''' your user name and password.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[record]] (something) in an [[account]], [[ledger]], etc.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2003|author=A. Mukherjee; M. Hanif|title=Financial Accounting|isbn=978-0-87083-038-9|pages=27|passage=Each amount '''entered''' in the debit column of the journal is posted by '''entering''' it on the credit side/column of an account in the ledger.}}
