## {{lb|en|figurative}} {{n-g|Used in the manner of a [[stage direction]]:}} to [[enter the picture]], to become [[relevant]].
##* {{quote-journal|en|date=2026-04-08|author=Megan Uy|title=12 Best Crossbody Bags for Travel That’ll Hold All Your Stuff Without Messing Up Your Vacay Outfit|journal=w:[[Cosmopolitan (magazine)|Cosmopolitan]]|url=https://www.cosmopolitan.com/style-beauty/fashion/g70884849/crossbody-bags-for-travel/|passage=I’m usually a shoulder bag kind of girl, just because it fits my vibe more. But when I’m on my feet for hours—running through crowded airports or touring a new city—the last thing I want to think about is my stuff. '''Enter''': A good crossbody.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20260920165606/https://www.cosmopolitan.com/style-beauty/fashion/g70884849/crossbody-bags-for-travel/|archivedate=20 September 2026}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive|law}} To become a [[party]] to an agreement, [[treaty]], etc.
#* {{quote-web|en|date=2003-2-4|author=The President of the United States|site=U.S. Government Printing Office|title=NOTIFICATION TO ENTER INTO A FREE TRADE AGREEMENT WITH THE GOVERNMENT OF SINGAPORE|url=http://www.gpo.gov/fdsys/pkg/CDOC-108hdoc29/html/CDOC-108hdoc29.htm|accessdate=2013-9-9
|passage=I am pleased to notify the Congress of my intent to '''enter''' into a Free Trade Agreement (FTA) with the Government of Singapore.}}
# {{lb|en|law|intransitive}} To become effective; to come into effect.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2005|author=United Nations|title=Dispositions Législatives Et Réglementaires Nationales Relatives À la Prévention Et À L'élimination Du Terrorisme International|isbn=978-92-1-033093-0|page=215|passage=This Act shall '''enter''' into force on 01 March 1998.}}
# {{lb|en|legal}} To go into or upon, as lands, and take actual possession of them.
# {{lb|en|transitive|legal}} To place in regular form before the court, usually in writing; to put upon record in proper from and order.<ref>{{R:Burrill Law Dictionary}}</ref>
#: {{ux|en|to '''enter''' a writ, appearance, rule, or judgment}}
# To make report of (a vessel or its cargo) at the [[custom house]]; to submit a statement of (imported goods), with the original invoices, to the proper customs officer for estimating the duties. See ''[[entry]]''.
# {{lb|en|transitive|US|dated|historical}} To [[file]], or [[register]] with the land office, the required particulars concerning (a quantity of public land) in order to entitle a person to a right of preemption.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1887|author=United States General Land Office|title=Annual Report of the Commissioner of General Land Office|publisher=US Government Printing Office|page=82|passage=Under existing laws governing the qualifications of an alien '''to enter''' 160 acres or more of the public domain he is only required to file his declaration of intent to become a citizen.}}
# To [[deposit]] for [[copyright]] the [[title]] or [[description]] of (a book, picture, map, etc.).
#: {{ux|en|'''entered''' according to act of Congress}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|obsolete}} To initiate; to introduce favourably.
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Antony and Cleopatra|passage=This sword but shown to Caesar, with this tidings, / Shall '''enter''' me with him.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive|formal}} To [[begin]] (a regular activity or job); to [[undertake]]; to [[take up]]. {{+obj|en|:on/:upon}}
#* {{RQ:Dickens Great Expectations|I|XII|199|{{...}} I '''entered''', that same day, on a regular occupation of pushing Miss Havisham in this chair {{...}} round her own room, and across the landing, and round the other room.}}

